    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests passing).\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a `telephoneDisplay` field that returns the stored E.164 telephone formatted for humans, while `telephone` stays raw E.164.\n\nChanges, each placed where the concern belongs:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the read-only `telephoneDisplay` property to the `Owner` schema (alongside the other derived fields like `displayName`/`initials`), so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it.\n\n2. **`util/CountryCallingCodes.java`** (new) \u2014 Extracted the country-calling-code catalog (`61\u21929`, `1\u219210`) plus a longest-prefix helper into a single source of truth. Previously this data lived privately inside `TelephoneNormalizer`; now both normalization and formatting share it rather than duplicating the code list.\n\n3. **`TelephoneNormalizer.java`** \u2014 Refactored to reuse `CountryCallingCodes` (its private map and bespoke longest-match logic are gone), preserving identical validation behavior.\n\n4. **`util/TelephoneDisplayFormatter.java`** (new) \u2014 Small single-responsibility formatter: splits the country code off (via the shared catalog) and groups the national digits in threes \u2192 `+61412345678` becomes `+61 412 345 678`. Returns `null` for an absent number.\n\n5. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `telephoneDisplay` mapping delegating to the formatter, matching the existing pattern of the other computed fields.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay` (input `0412 345 678` \u2192 `telephone` = `+61412345678`, `telephoneDisplay` = `+61 412 345 678`) passes.",
